cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: dataset
title: "So Many Ways to Multiply 3x3 Matrices: A Large Dataset of Rank-23 Schemes"
authors:
  - family-names: Perminov
    given-names: Andrew I.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8047-0114"
    affiliation: "Research Center for TAI Institute for System Programming"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dronperminov/rank23_3x3_dataset"
url: "https://github.com/dronperminov/rank23_3x3_dataset"
abstract: >-
  A dataset of tens of thousands of rank-23 schemes for 3x3 matrix
  multiplication in which every scheme has its own rank pattern, so all
  schemes are pairwise inequivalent. The schemes were obtained by a numerical
  method combining gradient descent with alternating least squares and by flip
  graph search, and have ternary, integer or rational coefficients. The dataset
  is provided in JSON, plain text and Maple formats together with a script
  that verifies the correctness of every scheme.
keywords:
  - 3x3 matrix multiplication
  - fast matrix multiplication
  - tensor decomposition
  - bilinear complexity
  - flip graphs
  - dataset
